@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Terms of service";
}

<section class="container py-5">
    <div class="row justify-content-center">
        <div class="col-lg-9">
            <div class="text-center mb-4" data-reveal>
                <span class="eyebrow">Legal</span>
                <h1 class="section-title mt-2">Terms of service</h1>
                <p class="section-lead mx-auto mt-2">Last updated 16 November 2026</p>
            </div>

            <div class="glass p-4 p-lg-5" data-reveal="80">
                <h2 class="h5 mt-0">1. The service</h2>
                <p class="text-muted-silver">
                    Nexus sells dial-up internet, broadband and landline services through approved retail partners.
                    The plan that is shown on the website is the plan that is installed. A service is only activated
                    after the feasibility survey has been passed.
                </p>

                <h2 class="h5">2. Orders and the feasibility survey</h2>
                <p class="text-muted-silver">
                    An order passes through the states <em>placed</em>, <em>feasibility pending</em>,
                    <em>feasible</em> or <em>not feasible</em> and finally <em>connection provided</em> or
                    <em>cancelled</em>. A dial-up order for a customer without a Nexus landline carries two checks -
                    the landline exchange and the internet server. If a check fails the order is closed as
                    <em>not feasible</em> and no connection is created.
                </p>

                <h2 class="h5">3. Prices, deposits and discounts</h2>
                <p class="text-muted-silver">
                    The price list is maintained by the administrator and is published on the website. The security
                    deposit is charged once on the activation invoice and is held on the deposit ledger of the
                    customer. Orders that carry several connections receive a bulk discount on the advance payment
                    and on the security deposit: 25 percent from 10 connections, 50 percent from 16, 75 percent from
                    26 and 100 percent from 51 connections.
                </p>

                <h2 class="h5">4. Invoices and payment</h2>
                <p class="text-muted-silver">
                    Nexus is a cash on delivery network. The activation invoice is settled with the installer, the
                    periodic bills are paid at the retail counter. The service tax of 12.24 percent is applied on the
                    discounted subtotal of every invoice. A bill that stays unpaid for more than 30 days flags the
                    connection as overdue and the line is switched to temporarily inactive until the dues are cleared.
                </p>

                <h2 class="h5">5. Equipment</h2>
                <p class="text-muted-silver">
                    The router, the modem and the telephone equipment remain the property of Nexus or of the
                    manufacturer. A replacement of a lost or damaged device is charged at the published replacement
                    price on the next invoice.
                </p>

                <h2 class="h5">6. Suspension and closure</h2>
                <p class="text-muted-silver">
                    A connection can be temporarily inactive while a bill is overdue and permanently inactive when
                    the customer leaves the service. The security deposit is refunded after the equipment has been
                    returned and the final bill has been settled.
                </p>

                <h2 class="h5">7. Acceptable use</h2>
                <p class="text-muted-silver">
                    The service may not be used for spam, for re-selling the access or for any activity that harms
                    the network. A violation leads to the suspension of the connection.
                </p>

                <h2 class="h5">8. Changes</h2>
                <p class="text-muted-silver">
                    Nexus may adjust the price list, the deposits, the discount bands and the tax rate. The values
                    that apply are always the ones that are stored in the settings of the system and that are shown
                    on the invoice that is issued.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>
